<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Passau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Passau is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-bavaria">Lower Bavaria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, where the Inn and the Ilz meet the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> near the Austrian border. Its bishopric, organised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-boniface">Saint Boniface</a> in 739, became one of the largest dioceses of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, reaching far down the Danube, and from 1217 its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> ruled the city and surrounding lands as prince-bishops until secularisation in 1803. St Stephen's Cathedral dominates its baroque old town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/passau.jpg" alt="Passau" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Compiled by Viceskeeni2 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PassauCollection2025.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
